-- title:
--   q-expansion field of Γ_H(M)∩Γ₀(Mℓ) equals that of Γ_{H'}(Mℓ)
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ and $\ell$ be natural numbers, both nonzero, and let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M\mathbb{Z})^\times$. The assertion is an equality of intermediate fields of the field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$, namely of $\mathbb{Q}$-subextensions generated by the sets `intFormRatiosC ℚ Γ` attached to two subgroups $\Gamma$ of $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$. On the left, [`ModularCurve.xHTopFunctionFieldC ℚ M H (M * ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L84) is by definition [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) of the group $\Gamma_H(M)\cap\Gamma_0(M\ell)$, where $\Gamma_H(M)$ is [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the image in $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism `gamma0Units M` on $\Gamma_0(M)$, and $\Gamma_0(M\ell)$ is the usual level-$M\ell$ group. On the right, [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (M * ℓ) H'`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) is [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) of $\Gamma_{H'}(M\ell)$, with $H'$ the subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M\ell\mathbb{Z})^\times$ obtained by pulling $H$ back along the reduction map `ZMod.unitsMap` for the divisibility $M \mid M\ell$. Thus the two intermediate fields, each generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ by the ratios of integral $q$-expansions attached to the respective group, coincide.
--
--   This identifies the $q$-expansion function field of the top curve $X(\Gamma_H(M)\cap\Gamma_0(M\ell))$ of the Hecke correspondence over $X_H(M)$ with the function field of the modular curve $X_{H'}(M\ell)$ for the pulled-back character group $H'$, so that results established for the fields [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) apply verbatim to the top curve. It is used in [`ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf.heckeDivHBar_single_pt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf.heckeDivHBar_single_pt).
